      "text": "To find the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of 18 and 42, we first need to determine both the GCD and the LCM of these two numbers. We will start by finding the prime factors of each number, use those factors to find the GCD and LCM.\n\n1. Start by finding the prime factors of each number:\n- The prime factors of 18 are \\(18 = 2 \\times 3^2\\).\n- The prime factors of 42 are \\(42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7\\).\n\n2. The GCD of two numbers is the product of the lowest power of all prime factors common to both numbers. So, the GCD of 18 and 42 = \\(2^1 \\times 3^1 = 6\\).\n\n3. The LCM of two numbers is the product of the highest power of all prime factors present in either number. So, the LCM of 18 and 42 = \\(2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 378\\).\n\n4. Now, we find the product of the GCD and the LCM of these two numbers:\n\\[ \\text{Product} = \\text{GCD}(18, 42) \\times \\text{LCM}(18, 42) = 6 \\times 378. \\]\n\n5. Let's calculate this:\n\\[ 6 \\times 378 = 2268. \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of 18 and 42 is \\(\\boxed{2268}\\).",
